verses.text:
“Blessed is God, the ever-living,
and blessed his reign!
For he chastises, and he shows mercy;
he brings down to Hades, to the lowest depths of the earth,
and he himself brings up from the great destruction;
there is nothing that can slip from his hand.

Here, in the country of my captivity, I praise him;
I proclaim his might and his majesty to a sinful people.{c}
Return, sinners, and act righteously in his sight;
who can tell? He may take pleasure in you and deal kindly with you.

I extol my God;
my soul extols heaven’s King
and will exult in his majesty.

A brilliant light will blaze to all the earth’s limits;
from afar a multitude of nations will come to you,
and the dwellers at the world’s remotest edges to your holy name,
carrying gifts in their hands for heaven’s King.
Age upon age will give exultation within you,
and the name of the elect city will last for every age to come.

Fortunate as well are all who mourned for you
because of every blow you bore;
for in you they will find joy,
and they will look on the fullness of your gladness forever.
Bless the Lord, my soul, the mighty King!
